    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "Scope Note: Insikt Group conducted interviews with a former Iranian hacker with first-hand knowledge of the information shared and was living in Iran when he started one of Iran’s first security forums.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "According to Insikt Group’s source, the Iranian government authorized denial-of-service attacks on America’s largest financial services companies as an immediate response to the sanctions in a campaign dubbed Operation Ababil .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_19",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "The Iranian attacks in 2012 and 2014 were in contrast to the relatively slow and methodical work of APT 33, APT 34, and APT 35, developing custom malware, targeting data exfiltration from strategic intelligence targets such as U.S.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_20",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s5"
      },
      "text": "military contractors, Middle East energy companies, and university research networks .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_21",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s6"
      },
      "text": "Comparing Iranian campaigns — methodical versus reactionary.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s2"
      },
      "text": "According to Insikt Group’s source, during the 2009 Green Revolution, Gerdab.ir emerged as the IRGC’s domestic hacking group tasked with targeting opposition news websites and individuals considered immoral by the regime.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s3"
      },
      "text": "According to Insikt Group’s source, the government answer was a tiered approach, with a network of people unofficially associated with the IRGC and Iranian government — a type of ideologically aligned middle management — that were loyal to the regime and demonstrated sufficient religious commitment.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_40",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s6"
      },
      "text": "This ongoing campaign, which targets universities for scientific and technological intellectual property theft, demonstrates a fundamental lack of trust in the international agreements, including the Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action (JCPOA) .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_43",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s9"
      },
      "text": "FireEye disclosed that the Nasr Institute was an APT 33 contractor in an operation that used publicly available backdoors and remote access trojans.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_44",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s10"
      },
      "text": "The handle “xman_1365_x” (self-identified on security forums as Mahdi Honarvar) was found by FireEye in malware artifacts, which open sources linked to the Nasr Institute.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_45",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s11"
      },
      "text": "The actor xman_1365_x was then linked to a security company called Kavosh Security via OSINT by Iran Cyber News Agency.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_46",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s12"
      },
      "text": "The actor was linked to a destructive operation, which used NewsBeef and StoneDrill malware families.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_48",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s1"
      },
      "text": "Command and control (C2) domains used by StoneDrill and NewsBeef in Kaspersky’s findings were found to share an SSL certificate, which surfaced an additional three domains in research by the Iran Cyber News Agency.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_49",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s2"
      },
      "text": "Additional publicly known Iranian contractors include ITSecTeam (ITSEC) and Mersad Company , also linked to Operation Ababil.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_50",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s3"
      },
      "text": "The links between the Iranian government and contractors are well documented; however, the identity of specific groups and individuals within the Iranian government and IRGC responsible for offensive cyber campaigns is murky, as is the relationship between contractors and security forums.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_52",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s5"
      },
      "text": "First, FireEye referenced the publicly available ALFA TEaM Shell in APT33 spear phishing email campaigns .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_54",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p9_s1"
      },
      "text": "Second, xman_1365_x created an Ashiyane profile on August 8, 2010, allegedly not long after Ashiyane temporarily became the primary security forum in Iran, following Behrooz Kamalian’s visit to prominent cleric, Ayatollah Naser Makarem Shirazi.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_55",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_cta-2018-0509(05-09-2018)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
